3:T124c,<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Dealing with knee pain can be a significant hurdle in your daily life. Advances in orthopedic surgery have made it possible to restore knee function and relieve pain through effective cartilage repair surgery. As we look towards 2026, several innovative treatment options are emerging, offering hope for patients suffering from knee cartilage damage. In Hyderabad, India, Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy, a highly esteemed Senior Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, provides expert guidance on the best cartilage repair surgery options available.</p>

<h2>Understanding Knee Cartilage Damage</h2>
<p>Knee cartilage acts as a cushion between the bones, enabling smooth movement and bearing the body's weight. However, injury or long-term wear and tear can lead to cartilage damage, resulting in pain, swelling, and restricted motion. Conditions such as osteoarthritis, sports injuries, and accidental trauma are common causes of cartilage deterioration. Recognizing the symptoms early and seeking expert orthopedic care is crucial for timely and effective treatment.</p>

<h2>Symptoms of Cartilage Damage</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Pain and discomfort during movement</li>
  <li>Swelling and tenderness around the knee</li>
  <li>Stiffness and reduced range of motion</li>
  <li>A grating sensation during joint movement</li>
</ul>

<h2>Treatment Options</h2>
<p>The latest treatment options for cartilage repair surgery in 2026 are transforming patient outcomes. Some of the most promising techniques include:</p>
<p><strong>1. Autologous Chondrocyte Implantation (ACI):</strong> This procedure involves harvesting healthy cartilage cells from the patient, growing them in a lab, and re-implanting them into the damaged area. ACI promotes natural cartilage regeneration, making it a personalized treatment method.</p>
<p><strong>2. Microfracture Surgery:</strong> A minimally invasive technique where small holes are created in the bone beneath the cartilage to stimulate new cartilage growth. This procedure is typically used for small areas of damage.</p>
<p><strong>3. Osteochondral Autograft Transplantation (OAT):</strong> In this method, healthy cartilage and underlying bone are transferred from a non-weight-bearing joint area to the damaged site, offering a quicker recovery for patients.</p>
<p><strong>4. Stem Cell Therapy:</strong> Leveraging stem cells' regenerative properties to facilitate cartilage repair. This cutting-edge treatment option shows promise in accelerating healing and restoring knee function.</p>
<p><strong>5. Biologic Injections:</strong> These include platelet-rich plasma (PRP) and growth factor injections designed to enhance healing and provide symptomatic relief.</p>

<h2>Why Choose Dr. Harsha at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</h2>
<p>When it comes to knee cartilage repair surgery, selecting a skilled and experienced surgeon is vital. Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy is renowned for his expertise in advanced orthopedic procedures. At Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, you are assured world-class care equipped with state-of-the-art medical technologies.</p>
<p>Dr. Harsha's extensive experience in cartilage repair surgery, along with his patient-centered approach, ensures that each patient receives personalized treatment plans tailored to their specific needs. This commitment to excellence has made him a trusted name in Hyderabad's orthopedic community.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How do I know if I need cartilage repair surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: If you experience persistent knee pain, swelling, or difficulty in motion that doesn't improve with conservative treatments, consult an orthopedic specialist like Dr. Harsha to evaluate your condition.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What is the recovery time for cartilage repair surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: Recovery time varies based on the specific procedure performed and individual health factors. Generally, patients can expect to resume normal activities within 3-6 months post-surgery, under the guidance of their orthopedic care team.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Are these treatments available at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</strong></p>
<p>A: Yes, all these advanced cartilage repair treatments are available at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, under the expert care of Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy.</p>

<h2>Book Your Appointment</h2>
<p>Reclaim your mobility and get relief from knee pain with the latest cartilage repair surgery treatments. Call Dr. Harsha at <strong>+91 99599 64567</strong> or visit Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Nanakramguda, Hyderabad for a consultation.</p>5:["slug","best-cartilage-repair-surgery-knee-guide-2026-latest-treatment-options-hyderabad","d"]
